<h1>About &amp; Disclaimer</h1>

<div class="alert alert-warning">
    <strong>Not tax advice.</strong> Taxing is a calculation aid. It does not constitute
    professional tax, legal or financial advice. Always verify every figure and consult a
    qualified Chartered Accountant before filing your return.
</div>

<h2>What it does</h2>
<p>
    Taxing helps a salaried resident of India (for example, a Microsoft India employee with
    Microsoft RSUs that vest into a US brokerage account) prepare the foreign-asset and
    foreign-income portions of ITR-2 / ITR-3:
</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Schedule FA — A2</strong>: foreign custodial (brokerage) account.</li>
    <li><strong>Schedule FA — A3</strong>: foreign equity &amp; debt interest (the held shares).</li>
    <li><strong>Schedule FSI</strong>: foreign source income (dividends).</li>
    <li><strong>Schedule TR</strong> and <strong>Form 67</strong>: relief for foreign tax paid.</li>
    <li><strong>Schedule CG</strong>: capital gains on share sales (FIFO lot matching).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Key conventions</h2>
<ul>
    <li>
        <strong>Reporting periods.</strong> Schedule FA uses the calendar year (1 Jan – 31 Dec);
        income schedules use the financial year (1 Apr – 31 Mar).
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Currency conversion.</strong> Income is converted per <strong>Rule 128</strong>
        using the SBI TT buying rate on the last day of the month preceding the month of
        accrual. Schedule FA balances are valued at the SBI TTBR on the valuation date, with a
        preceding-working-day fallback for holidays.
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Capital gains.</strong> Foreign/unlisted shares are long-term when held more than
        24 months. Cost equals the vesting fair-market value (already taxed as a perquisite),
        preventing double taxation.
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>Privacy &amp; security</h2>
<ul>
    <li>All parsing and calculation run entirely in your browser (WebAssembly).</li>
    <li>Your statement is never uploaded to any server and is cleared when you close the tab.</li>
    <li>Account numbers are masked (all but the last four digits) in every output.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Limitations</h2>
<ul>
    <li>SBI TTBR rates shipped with the app are illustrative samples — supply official rates.</li>
    <li>
        Schedule FA peak/closing balances are approximated from securities value plus cash;
        verify against your broker's own peak-value statement.
    </li>
    <li>Provide a 31 December market price per symbol for accurate closing valuations.</li>
</ul>
